---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';

const repo = 'https://github.com/jitendraag/cn-at-scaler';
---

<Base title="About">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This site is an unofficial study companion for the course Network Architecture (CN @ Scaler). A student of the
    course built it. The instructor and the school did not make it, and they do not check it.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    A live lecture moves fast, and one missed idea makes the next one hard to follow. So this site teaches the course
    again, one idea at a time, in the order of the sessions. Each lesson starts with a scene from real life that a
    10-year-old can follow. Then it goes deep enough for the exam and for design questions. Questions along the way show
    what you know, and a review queue brings each idea back over the next days.
  </p>

  <h2>Two rules it keeps</h2>
  <p>
    The first rule: it gives no solutions to graded work. Graded work is the calculator assignment, the binary HTTP
    project and the real questions of the post-class quizzes. A page that helps you prepare for graded work gives a
    checklist, a test plan and hints. It never gives the answer or the code.
  </p>
  <p>
    The second rule: every fact comes from a source that you can check. The source is the slides, the instructor code,
    or a named reference such as an RFC or a manual page. A fact that is not in the slides carries a "beyond the slides"
    badge with its reference. If a lesson and the slides do not agree, trust the slides, and ask the instructor.
  </p>

  <h2>Your progress stays with you</h2>
  <p>
    The site has no accounts and no analytics. Your answers and your review cards live only in this browser, at this
    address. If you clear the browser data, or move to a new browser or device, your progress stays behind. So export it
    from time to time on the <a href={href('progress/')}>Progress page</a>, and import the file in the new place.
  </p>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  <p>
    The slides and the demo code belong to the instructor. Every demo in the lessons comes from the instructor repo,{' '}
    <a href={repo}>github.com/jitendraag/cn-at-scaler</a>. The <a href={href('slides/')}>Slides page</a> has the deck of
    each session, to view here or to download.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }
</style>
